Nmap for Host Discovery & Network Scanning:
-------------------------------------------

-> Introduction to Nmap:
------------------------

    => Nmap (Network Mapper) is an open-source network discovery and security auditing tool used to identify:

        -> Live hosts on a network
        -> Open, closed, and filtered ports
        -> Running network services
        -> Service versions
        -> Operating systems
        -> Network configurations
        -> Potential security weaknesses

    => Nmap is widely used by:

        -> Network administrators
        -> Cybersecurity professionals
        -> Penetration testers
        -> Ethical hackers
        -> Security researchers
        -> System administrators

    => The primary purpose of Nmap is network discovery and security assessment.

*** Important: Nmap should only be used against systems and networks for which you have explicit authorization.
